#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059527 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059714 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6b4ebe4-9baa-5ff0-847a-49d99ba69795" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given in Component Form"}] :question/id #uuid "e2b211fe-d37a-55dd-bf76-9ffab2b6f128" :question/math-academy-id "e-4297" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle -4, 6 \\rangle$. Find $\\mid \\,\\mathbf{a}\\, \\mid$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid a \\mid &= \\sqrt{a_{x}^{2} + a_{y}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-4)^{2} + (6)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{16 + 36} \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt{13}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059528 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059715 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bc170fa-a70e-55af-8f3e-f4ea07431e30" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector From Position Vectors and then Computing its Magnitude"}] :question/id #uuid "d4ad6011-24a4-5642-997f-dcc4e807224f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4298" :question/problem "Let $A(1,3)$ and $B(2,-2)$. Find $\\mid \\overrightarrow{AB} \\mid$.\n\n![](images/f9/f95ee3c5c81750d97019d910350e4c78f0962baa682c834928450a451691145a.png)" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\nOA^(→) = a = i + 3j,; OB^(→) = b = 2i - 2j\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB^(→) &= OB^(→) - OA^(→) \\\\\n&= b - a \\\\\n&= (2i - 2j) - (i + 3j) \\\\\n&= i - 5j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid AB^(→) \\mid &= \\sqrt{1^{2} + (-5)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{1 + 25} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{26}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059530 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059716 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c45a70b-273c-5fec-a768-40a1cf218628" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "65198cdd-dd3b-5840-aaf3-cecd96eb9d3b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4301" :question/problem "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{a + 2b}{\\mid a + 2b \\mid}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na + 2b &= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + 2 \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 + 2 \\\\ 0 + (-2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid a + 2b \\mid &= \\sqrt{0^{2} + (-2)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4} \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{a + 2b}{\\mid a + 2b \\mid} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(a + 2b) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059716 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c45a70b-273c-5fec-a768-40a1cf218628" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1069ee09-17b5-57ab-aab5-38e6b996e90c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572841} {:answer/id #uuid "20e6eaac-82d9-5705-8448-025257524e8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572863} {:answer/id #uuid "79a93776-a59c-5551-bd4b-8aac720a2d40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572980} {:answer/id #uuid "a81428f3-9e59-5a07-9500-76476f5034a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573037} {:answer/id #uuid "acc576d0-0654-519c-b96b-6398ec344ad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{5\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ -\\frac{6}{5\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79a93776-a59c-5551-bd4b-8aac720a2d40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572980} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad9dfc42-a7b2-570f-831f-bdb8b850c4c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573211}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "efcda90e-97e9-5de4-ab6e-f342fb013418" :question/math-academy-id "q-125137" :question/problem "Let $r=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $r$ and points the same direction." :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{r}{|\\,r\\,|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,r\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{45} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $r$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{r}{|r|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{5}}\\cdot r \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{5}}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573287 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059714 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6b4ebe4-9baa-5ff0-847a-49d99ba69795" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given in Component Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06f4878d-2b22-5080-b71d-e44372f2d016" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572833} {:answer/id #uuid "3f5f3505-15b1-548f-bc68-5dc8b5cd1856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572897} {:answer/id #uuid "87f5f51b-4856-5dc0-b0e5-2f3c355ea3be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572997} {:answer/id #uuid "94a4df81-f598-5b1a-8c7c-7dfe90337b8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573016} {:answer/id #uuid "c114d74b-8feb-5637-9c93-f0e010981f98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f5f3505-15b1-548f-bc68-5dc8b5cd1856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572897} :answer-field/id #uuid "20e48ca9-80f3-5bdd-beed-e52606176cac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84731c4b-0fa0-51b7-ab58-c2cc224240fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-1307" :question/problem "If $u=⟨2,3⟩$, then what is the magnitude of $u?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,u\\,| & =\\sqrt{{u}_{x}^{2}+{u}_{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059714 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6b4ebe4-9baa-5ff0-847a-49d99ba69795" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given in Component Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18d115c9-84d2-581b-ae54-3c5a392028f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572849} {:answer/id #uuid "416bf8df-8b35-5b3b-8251-fed7dfc9545a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{31}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572901} {:answer/id #uuid "5f6db638-2f62-5677-827d-ee425c9aafcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572933} {:answer/id #uuid "a3449bba-2a92-58bc-975c-d54b2afa32da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573033} {:answer/id #uuid "ec43eb77-641f-58c3-9a18-ba04193242f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3449bba-2a92-58bc-975c-